    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-username>/maes"
abstract: >
  MAES is a single-file Python multi-agent ALife simulator (NumPy only)
  that studies emergent cognitive ecology, dimensional abduction, and
  communication layers. Built on a hands-off methodology: the experimenter
  sets initial conditions and observes; the simulator does not optimize
  for any goal. Phase 1 empirical study (80 runs, 4 conditions x 20 seeds)
  demonstrates that dimensional abduction (5D->13D) approximately doubles
  ai_peak and yields ~9x increase in species diversity, supporting the
  central architectural claim.
keywords:
  - artificial-life
  - multi-agent-systems
  - open-ended-evolution
  - dimensional-abduction
  - cognitive-ecology
  - emergent-communication
  - hands-off-methodology
